  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "What the solver actually uses", "items": [
      "SubjectRequirements generate demand per matching grade/class; locked occurrences reduce required demand.",
      "Teacher class eligibility, optional subject whitelist, weekly cap and unavailable slots constrain placement.",
      "Teacher and class double-booking are prevented for generated placements; break periods are skipped.",
      "Search is bounded at approximately 200,000 steps. Failure triggers greedy fallback and an explicit unsolved-demand warning."
    ] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Drafts, locks and editing", "items": [
      "Generate and Reset Draft delete unlocked lessons; locked lessons survive. Locks are not an authorization barrier to manual edit/clear.",
      "Manual save stores a lesson even when conflict checks find errors. Empty subject AND class removes the existing cell.",
      "Manual save checks the lesson and rescans same-slot neighbours; this is not a full timetable-wide rescan.",
      "The UI uses three hard-coded demo teacher profiles and a fixed TP 2025/2026, ALL definition; collaborator presence is static.",
      "Teacher view edits cells; class, room and master views project stored lessons. Room checks exist, but this cell picker does not assign rooms."
